oximately 94% in FY26 (FY25: 94%) and total revenue increased by 11% to \u20ac15.54bn, up from \u20ac13.95bn in FY25.","k":"sell"},{"t":"Ancillary Revenues accounted for approximately 32% of Ryanair\u2019s total operating revenues in FY26 and approximately 34% in FY25.","k":"sell"},{"t":"Forward-looking statements with regard to the Company\u2019s business rely on a number of assumptions concerning future events and are subject to a number of uncertainties and other factors, many of which are outside the Company\u2019s control, that could cause actual results to differ materially from such statements.","k":"buy"},{"t":"The success of its business model depends on its ability to control costs so as to deliver low fares while at the same time earning a profit.","k":"buy"},{"t":"Ryanair\u2019s future growth also materially depends on its ability to access suitable airports located in its targeted geographic markets at costs that are consistent with Ryanair\u2019s strategy.","k":"buy"},{"t":"O\u2019Leary.\u201d Ryanair\u2019s success also depends on the ability of its Executive Officers and other members of senior management to operate and manage effectively, both independently and as a Group.","k":"buy"},{"t":"Passenger airlines generally rely on travel agents (whether traditional or online) for a significant portion of their ticket sales and pay travel agents\u2019 commission for their services, as well as reimbursing them for the fees charged by reservation systems providers.","k":"buy"},{"t":"For additional information, please see \u201cItem 3\u2014Key information\u2014Risk Factors\u2014Risks related to the Company\u2014A majority of Ryanair\u2019s aircraft and certain parts are sourced from a single supplier; therefore, Ryanair would be materially and adversely affected if such supplier was unable to provide additional equipment or support\u201d.","k":"buy"},{"t":"Slot values depend on several factors, including the airport, time of day covered, the availability of slots and the class of aircraft.","k":"buy"},{"t":"Cash generated from operations was the primary source of cash inflows in FY26.","k":"buy"},{"t":"Cash generated from operations were the primary sources of cash inflows for FY25.","k":"buy"},{"t":"The Company relies on certain exemptions from the Nasdaq corporate governance rules.","k":"buy"},{"t":"Principal sources of estimation uncertainty have been set forth below.","k":"buy"},{"t":"The Group had purchased sufficient carbon credits to satisfy the FY26 emissions and as such, the cost of emissions is not deemed to represent a major source of estimation uncertainty.","k":"buy"},{"t":"In these hedge relationships, the main sources of ineffectiveness are changes in the timing of the hedged transactions.","k":"buy"},{"t":"In these hedging relationships the main sources of ineffectiveness are changes in the timing of the hedged transactions.","k":"buy"},{"t":"Cash generated from operations has been the principal source for these cash requirements during the year.","k":"buy"}],"x":[]},"std":"IFRS"}